From 7688993d40b6134fe18459bc5d696a83353b5528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azeem Shaikh <azeemshaikh38@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 16 May 2023 02:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 251/744] scsi: qla2xxx: Replace all non-returning strlcpy()
 with strscpy()

[ Upstream commit 37f1663c91934f664fb850306708094a324c227c ]

strlcpy() reads the entire source buffer first.  This read may exceed the
destination size limit.  This is both inefficient and can lead to linear
read overflows if a source string is not NUL-terminated [1].  In an effort
to remove strlcpy() completely [2], replace strlcpy() here with strscpy().
No return values were used, so direct replacement is safe.

