From de71930136ce130503373fcaf33fbb987e999a1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Feb 2022 15:48:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 730/744] ipv6: annotate some data-races around sk->sk_prot

commit 086d49058cd8471046ae9927524708820f5fd1c7 upstream.

IPv6 has this hack changing sk->sk_prot when an IPv6 socket
is 'converted' to an IPv4 one with IPV6_ADDRFORM option.

This operation is only performed for TCP and UDP, knowing
their 'struct proto' for the two network families are populated
in the same way, and can not disappear while a reader
might use and dereference sk->sk_prot.

If we think about it all reads of sk->sk_prot while
either socket lock or RTNL is not acquired should be using READ_ONCE().

Also note that other layers like MPTCP, XFRM, CHELSIO_TLS also
write over sk->sk_prot.

BUG: KCSAN: data-race in inet6_recvmsg / ipv6_setsockopt

